A||||5||Rare87GT||Trunk switch=brake light inside?||||1||
Z||000000||Rare87GT||11-09-2001||11:12 AM||||My trunk switch button was working when I bought the car, now the brak light comes on inside my car.  I didn't know what I needed to do to fix it?  <P>------------------<BR>1987 GT *5 Speed*<BR>(Canadian Car)<BR>2.8L Mods--No Cat, K&N||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||11-09-2001||12:22 PM||||The two aren't connected - two totally separate things. If your brake light comes on when the e-brake is fully released, remove the boot over the ebrake handle and adjust the switch......<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||11-09-2001||01:22 PM||||Actually, the two may be connected.  I'm not sure about the 87's, but on the 88's the trunk release is wired such that the release relay gets its ground through the parking brake switch.  This is to prevent the release from working unless the parking brake is applied.  Maybe something is getting a ground somewhere it shouldn't.<BR>By the way, this only applies to manual transmission cars, the automatic gets its ground through the park/neutral switch.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000003||WhiteFieroBlur||11-09-2001||03:52 PM||||I have a manual 87 and I am having the same problem. When I have the car on my trunk will not pop. But if I turn the car off the trunk will pop. Also When I press the button to pop the trunk the brake light comes on. I have not a clue whats wrong.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-10-2001||02:24 PM||||The manual transmission cars with power trunk latch are wired so that hopefully you won't open the deck lid while moving... Since they have no park switch like an auto, Pontiac did some tricks with the brake handle.<P>In other words... there's probably nothing wrong. It could be the hand brake switch is messed up in the first post... or it could be you haven't quite got the operation figured out...<P>I think with the engine on the hand brake has to be pulled to open the deck. It's hard to tell from the wiring diagram.... I don't have one to test.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodrv6||11-10-2001||04:28 PM||||My 88 will open with the engine on or off IF the handbrake is applied.  The way the print looks, if you press the switch with the parking brake released, the relay will try and find a ground through the parking brake light.  I'll have to try that on the car and see what happens.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
